findings.suggested_fix:
Distinguish the two failure modes instead of discarding all of them. Keep discarding every other error (which is what makes `/dev/full` match), but on `ErrorKind::BrokenPipe` terminate with the status a SIGPIPE death produces:

```rust
if let Err(e) = writeln!(out, "{}", path.size()) {
    if e.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::BrokenPipe {
        std::process::exit(141); // 128 + SIGPIPE, as the C++ binary reports
    }
    // any other error: ignored, matching std::cout setting badbit and returning 0
}
```

This makes `$?` agree in the shell-pipeline case. It is still not bit-identical at the `waitpid` level (`WIFEXITED` vs `WIFSIGNALED`); reproducing that exactly would need `signal(SIGPIPE, SIG_DFL)`, which is not reachable from std alone, so if the residual difference is accepted it should be documented as a known limitation rather than claimed as agreement (see the related comment finding).
